# Laptop Exec — SSHFS Fast Path (auto)

Code on this server often lives under `~/mounts/<project>/` — SSHFS over a reverse
tunnel from the developer laptop. **Do not ask the user to mention laptop-exec.**

## Detect SSHFS workspace

Apply this rule when **any** of these is true:

- Workspace or file path contains `/mounts/`
- You would run bulk I/O: `find`, `rg`/`grep -r`, `git status/diff`, `dotnet build`, `npm test`
- A `find` over the project is taking more than a few seconds

**STOP:** If you are about to run `find`, `rg`, `git`, `dotnet build`, `npm test`,
or use the **Grep/Glob tool** on a path under `/mounts/`, use `laptop-exec` instead.
No exceptions. A Cursor hook blocks violations — do not retry direct commands.

Check session: `laptop-exec status` (requires connect.bat/sh on laptop).

## Mandatory split

| Task | Use | Never |
|------|-----|-------|
| Read/edit one file | Normal Read/Write on workspace path | — |
| **File count** | `laptop-exec run -- powershell -NoProfile -Command "(Get-ChildItem -Recurse -File -EA SilentlyContinue \| Measure-Object).Count"` | `find ... \| wc -l` on `/mounts/` |
| git status/diff/commit/push | `laptop-exec git -- …` | `git` in `~/mounts/...` |
| build / test / run | `laptop-exec run -- dotnet build` etc. | build on `~/mounts/...` |
| Read file from laptop | `laptop-exec read path/to/file` | — |

## Commands (default project = active connect session)

```bash
laptop-exec status
laptop-exec test                    # 7 self-tests; run if unsure
laptop-exec git -- status
laptop-exec git -- diff --stat
laptop-exec rg PATTERN
laptop-exec read scripts/foo.sh
laptop-exec run -- dotnet build
laptop-exec run -p OTHER_ID -- …    # other registered project
```

## If tunnel is DOWN

Tell user to run connect.bat/sh. Until then: single-file read/edit only; no bulk find/build.

## Why

Benchmarked on this infra: SSHFS `find` 23s+ cold; laptop-exec ~0.2s. SSHFS build often hangs.
